    "repo": "swesmith/iterative__dvc.1d6ea681",
    "problem_statement": "`dvc destroy` leaves `.dvcignore` behind\nThe title is pretty self-explanatory but when invoking the `dvc destroy` command, the `.dvcignore` file is left behind. Is this behaviour intentional?\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ dvc init\r\n$ echo foo > foo\r\n$ dvc add foo\r\n$ ls -a\r\n.dvc       .dvcignore .git       .gitignore foo        foo.dvc\r\n\r\n$ dvc destroy\r\nThis will destroy all information about your pipelines, all data files...\r\nAre you sure you want to continue?\r\nyes\r\n\r\n$ ls -a\r\n.dvcignore .git       .gitignore foo\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Version\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ dvc --version\r\n2.9.3\r\n\r\n$ sw_vers\r\nProductName:\tmacOS\r\nProductVersion:\t12.2\r\nBuildVersion:\t21D49\r\n```\n"
  }
